    "user_request_original": "Design and optimize a 24-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2 (24 finite layers total). Initialize thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness for 550 nm reference wavelength (HfO2: ~68.75 nm, SiO2: ~94.83 nm assuming n_HfO2≈2.0, n_SiO2≈1.46). Apply ±20% perturbation bounds around initialization values. Use simulated annealing optimizer with temperature schedule over first 50 iterations to enable cross-basin exploration. Optimize for mean transmittance maximization in 1530-1565 nm band and mean reflectance maximization in 400-700 nm band at normal unpolarized incidence. Treat all layers as coherent. Compute spectrum from 400-1565 nm with sufficient resolution to capture both bands. Include relative uniform thickness tolerance analysis for robustness scoring. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1530-1565 nm, 400-700 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 1530-1565 nm band; High reflectance in 400-700 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band; Low transmittance in 400-700 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 30.",
